789
00:31:35.060 --> 00:31:38.360
but the culture war is afoot.

790
00:31:38.360 --> 00:31:39.647
It is alive and well.

791
00:31:39.647 --> 00:31:42.120
Are we really gonna step into this?

792
00:31:42.120 --> 00:31:43.280
Very, very gingerly.

793
00:31:43.280 --> 00:31:44.500
There's no winners.

794
00:31:44.500 --> 00:31:45.333
Nobody wins in this space.

795
00:31:45.333 --> 00:31:46.297
By talking about this.

796
00:31:46.297 --> 00:31:47.547
No, no, nobody wins in this space.

797
00:31:47.547 --> 00:31:49.560
But it is what's happening right now,

798
00:31:49.560 --> 00:31:53.640
and I guess I feel like it's on a lot of people's minds.

799
00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:56.240
And I know that people have reached out to me,

800
00:31:56.240 --> 00:31:59.630
they'd like me to offer some thoughts about this,

801
00:31:59.630 --> 00:32:03.740
which I have some trepidation around

802
00:32:03.740 --> 00:32:06.150
because I'm not one for advice.

803
00:32:06.150 --> 00:32:07.640
If there's one thing that I've learned,

804
00:32:07.640 --> 00:32:10.053
and I learned this in recovery early and often,

805
00:32:14.400 --> 00:32:15.900
I'm reluctant to give advice.

806
00:32:15.900 --> 00:32:18.840
I'm somebody who likes to share

807
00:32:18.840 --> 00:32:21.450
from a perspective of experience.

808
00:32:21.450 --> 00:32:24.830
So I try to steer clear of treading in waters

809
00:32:24.830 --> 00:32:26.483
where I'm not an expert.

810
00:32:27.643 --> 00:32:31.727
So we're gonna talk about this perhaps briefly

811
00:32:33.060 --> 00:32:36.340
and as kind of gently as we can.

812
00:32:36.340 --> 00:32:38.093
But I think, as many people know,

813
00:32:39.530 --> 00:32:41.730
there's this controversy that's occurred

814
00:32:41.730 --> 00:32:44.090
over the last several days

815
00:32:44.090 --> 00:32:49.090
where Joe Rogan is sort of in the midst of a crossfire

816
00:32:51.410 --> 00:32:55.010
over particularly recent podcast episodes

817
00:32:55.010 --> 00:32:57.910
with McCullough and Malone

818
00:32:57.910 --> 00:33:02.470
these, I don't know how you would characterize them,

819
00:33:02.470 --> 00:33:07.470
doctors with non-mainstream opinions about vaccination.

820
00:33:09.910 --> 00:33:14.000
And the result of these conversations

821
00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:16.860
have caused certain artists out there

822
00:33:16.860 --> 00:33:19.610
to decide to pull their music from Spotify,

823
00:33:19.610 --> 00:33:24.100
which has put Spotify in this position of needing to

824
00:33:24.100 --> 00:33:27.310
or feeling like they have to respond to this.

825
00:33:27.310 --> 00:33:29.730
And Spotify, as of yesterday,

826
00:33:29.730 --> 00:33:33.730
had published a blog post by Daniel Ek, their CEO,

827
00:33:33.730 --> 00:33:37.810
wherein he kind of disclosed publicly for the first time

828
00:33:37.810 --> 00:33:40.920
these content guidelines and how they're going to,

829
00:33:40.920 --> 00:33:45.650
I guess, label certain conversations from time to time

830
00:33:45.650 --> 00:33:50.650
that are potentially in that misinformation space.

831
00:33:50.890 --> 00:33:54.350
And so, of course, this has caused quite the outbreak

832
00:33:54.350 --> 00:33:58.220
of opinionated puppet masters out there.

833
00:33:58.220 --> 00:34:00.433
What is your take on this?

834
00:34:01.390 --> 00:34:03.840
Well, I mean, not just opinions,

835
00:34:03.840 --> 00:34:07.810
but like Spotify's stock went down 6% at one point.

836
00:34:07.810 --> 00:34:10.760
Yeah, I think they lost $4 billion in market share,

837
00:34:10.760 --> 00:34:12.400
and there's other factors.

838
00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:14.210
I don't think you can just point

839
00:34:14.210 --> 00:34:16.240
to the Joe Rogan controversy

840
00:34:16.240 --> 00:34:18.140
and say this is all because of that.

841
00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:20.375
No, I think it was Barry Manilow getting involved.

842
00:34:20.375 --> 00:34:21.528
Is that what--

843
00:34:21.528 --> 00:34:22.597
Yeah, 'cause first it was Neil Young, then Barry Manilow.

844
00:34:22.597 --> 00:34:24.927
But then Barry Manilow tweeted the other day like,

845
00:34:24.927 --> 00:34:26.430
"I don't know what people are talking about.

846
00:34:26.430 --> 00:34:27.840
I haven't said anything about this."

847
00:34:27.840 --> 00:34:30.451
Oh, I'm sorry that was some misinformation on my part.

848
00:34:30.451 --> 00:34:32.480
There's misinformation right there.

849
00:34:32.480 --> 00:34:35.320
Barry Manilow fake news.

850
00:34:35.320 --> 00:34:36.730
He was brought into this somehow.

851
00:34:36.730 --> 00:34:38.313
Yeah, I know.

852
00:34:38.313 --> 00:34:39.720
So you have to take all of this with a little bit

853
00:34:39.720 --> 00:34:41.090
of a grain of salt.
Right.

854
00:34:41.090 --> 00:34:44.163
Well, my theory on all of this stuff is,

855
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.584
first, there's only one kind of free speech.

856
00:34:49.584 --> 00:34:54.380
And so either in favor of free speech,

857
00:34:54.380 --> 00:34:56.790
whether that's free speech moderated by companies

858
00:34:56.790 --> 00:34:59.920
or free speech moderated by governments, or you're not

859
00:34:59.920 --> 00:35:03.840
and you wanna control speech in some way.

860
00:35:03.840 --> 00:35:08.593
And I'm in favor of free speech, and may the best ideas win.

861
00:35:10.160 --> 00:35:13.020
And secondly, I don't think Joe Rogan traffics

862
00:35:13.020 --> 00:35:14.630
intentionally in misinformation.

863
00:35:14.630 --> 00:35:16.046
So that's the other thing.

864
00:35:16.046 --> 00:35:18.610
He might have opinions that differ from people,

865
00:35:18.610 --> 00:35:20.150
he might be a libertarian,

866
00:35:20.150 --> 00:35:22.730
remember, he was pro Bernie Sanders also at one point,

867
00:35:22.730 --> 00:35:26.190
so he's got very interesting viewpoints,

868
00:35:26.190 --> 00:35:31.040
but he's not, we're not comparing him to Fox News anchors

869
00:35:31.040 --> 00:35:33.790
that are intentionally muddying the waters

870
00:35:33.790 --> 00:35:35.830
and causing disinformation.

871
00:35:35.830 --> 00:35:39.260
I hold him in a completely different space,

872
00:35:39.260 --> 00:35:40.760
and I don't go to him for medical advice.

873
00:35:40.760 --> 00:35:43.840
So those are my ultimate opinions on that.

874
00:35:43.840 --> 00:35:46.370
And I think that in this culture war,

875
00:35:46.370 --> 00:35:49.070
we are trapped between the righteous and the ignorant.

876
00:35:49.960 --> 00:35:51.920
Those are the two loud viewpoints that we have.

877
00:35:51.920 --> 00:35:53.650
We have the righteous, the self-righteous,

878
00:35:53.650 --> 00:35:56.193
and we have the malevolent, malevolent,

879
00:35:58.238 --> 00:36:02.090
the malevolence of ignorance on the other.

880
00:36:02.090 --> 00:36:04.570
And it's not that fun to be in that space,

881
00:36:04.570 --> 00:36:07.410
because it's loud and it's disorienting

882
00:36:07.410 --> 00:36:09.300
and most of us are not there.

883
00:36:09.300 --> 00:36:10.960
Most of us are somewhere in the middle.

884
00:36:10.960 --> 00:36:12.970
We can handle differing opinions.

885
00:36:12.970 --> 00:36:14.763
We can figure out what to believe.

886
00:36:15.660 --> 00:36:19.030
And the funny part about being, between those two poles,

887
00:36:19.030 --> 00:36:22.300
is that on social media we all toggle between them.

888
00:36:22.300 --> 00:36:23.550
We can all be righteous

889
00:36:23.550 --> 00:36:26.035
and we can all be a little bit ignorant.

890
00:36:26.035 --> 00:36:29.600
And so when we do that,

891
00:36:29.600 --> 00:36:33.833
when we make the people who have dissenting opinions,

892
00:36:35.040 --> 00:36:36.910
we try to, when we try to snuff them out,

893
00:36:36.910 --> 00:36:40.070
we make them heroes, we make them the anti-establishment,

894
00:36:40.070 --> 00:36:42.400
we make them the punk rockers.

895
00:36:42.400 --> 00:36:44.163
We turn people like Matt Gaetz,

896
00:36:45.388 --> 00:36:48.600
who is the most punchable face in America, into a hero

897
00:36:48.600 --> 00:36:50.440
for all sorts of young people out there

898
00:36:50.440 --> 00:36:52.817
that are looking at the mainstream culture and thinking,

899
00:36:52.817 --> 00:36:56.290
"No," and that it's dangerous.

900
00:36:56.290 --> 00:36:59.600
That's why the Balinese have this culture,

901
00:36:59.600 --> 00:37:02.970
cultural idea of you can't crush the darkness.

902
00:37:02.970 --> 00:37:04.420
There's light and there's darkness,

903
00:37:04.420 --> 00:37:05.960
and you can't try to obliterate it.

904
00:37:05.960 --> 00:37:07.500
That's the point of free speech.

905
00:37:07.500 --> 00:37:11.000
You can't try to knock it out entirely.

906
00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:12.270
It's impossible.

907
00:37:12.270 --> 00:37:14.210
That's why you have to cherish speech

908
00:37:14.210 --> 00:37:15.740
and let everybody talk,

909
00:37:15.740 --> 00:37:17.670
because then that only helps you figure out

910
00:37:17.670 --> 00:37:19.000
the best way to go forward.

911
00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:20.860
I know it's a challenging time,

912
00:37:20.860 --> 00:37:22.890
but that's really the only way.

913
00:37:22.890 --> 00:37:25.350
Because when you ridicule people

914
00:37:25.350 --> 00:37:27.070
like Aaron Rodgers and Kyrie Irving

915
00:37:27.070 --> 00:37:28.380
and these people who have these,

916
00:37:28.380 --> 00:37:31.150
like you said, non-mainstream opinions about vaccines,

917
00:37:31.150 --> 00:37:34.500
you make them heroes, you actually elevate them.

918
00:37:34.500 --> 00:37:36.040
And that's the problem.

919
00:37:36.040 --> 00:37:37.280
The Streisand effect.

920
00:37:37.280 --> 00:37:38.860
The Streisand effect.
Yeah.

921
00:37:38.860 --> 00:37:43.860
How do you feel about Spotify's declarations

922
00:37:43.992 --> 00:37:48.992
around content moderation, and labeling, and the like?

923
00:37:50.130 --> 00:37:53.680
I mean, they're sort of taking a page

924
00:37:53.680 --> 00:37:55.631
out of the Facebook playbook like,

925
00:37:55.631 --> 00:37:59.470
"Are you just a distribution platform

926
00:37:59.470 --> 00:38:01.750
or are you a publisher,"

927
00:38:01.750 --> 00:38:04.900
and that's a very difficult situation to be in.

928
00:38:04.900 --> 00:38:08.870
It's almost an impossible situation for Spotify.

929
00:38:08.870 --> 00:38:12.680
I don't see them like kicking Rogan off the platform.

930
00:38:12.680 --> 00:38:13.930
I don't think that's gonna happen,

931
00:38:13.930 --> 00:38:16.250
nor do I think that they should do that.

932
00:38:16.250 --> 00:38:18.300
So they kind of issued this

933
00:38:18.300 --> 00:38:22.107
somewhat toothless response about,

934
00:38:22.107 --> 00:38:23.610
"Well, we're gonna do a better job

935
00:38:23.610 --> 00:38:25.990
of putting labels on things from time to time,

936
00:38:25.990 --> 00:38:28.400
or pulling things that clearly violate

937
00:38:28.400 --> 00:38:31.010
our relatively vague policy."

938
00:38:31.010 --> 00:38:31.843
Right.

939
00:38:31.843 --> 00:38:33.597
Well, I like the label because then I could just say,

940
00:38:33.597 --> 00:38:36.550
"Oh, he's gonna talk about COVID-19, I won't tune in."

941
00:38:36.550 --> 00:38:37.383
(both laugh)

942
00:38:37.383 --> 00:38:38.593
I feel like I'm getting enough COVID information.

943
00:38:38.593 --> 00:38:41.440
I don't need to actively seek out more.

944
00:38:41.440 --> 00:38:43.475
That's what's so weird, is, like,

945
00:38:43.475 --> 00:38:45.010
there's a lot of people making a living

946
00:38:45.010 --> 00:38:47.430
off of screaming and yelling about COVID.

947
00:38:47.430 --> 00:38:48.263
Well, sure.

948
00:38:48.263 --> 00:38:50.620
And the incentives are set up

949
00:38:50.620 --> 00:38:53.230
such that, particularly on Twitter,

950
00:38:53.230 --> 00:38:55.410
there's no incentive to be nuanced

951
00:38:55.410 --> 00:38:57.070
and balanced about anything.

952
00:38:57.070 --> 00:39:02.070
You're rewarded for outrage on both sides of this spectrum.

953
00:39:02.180 --> 00:39:05.783
So with the exception of the occasional super long thread,

954
00:39:06.680 --> 00:39:11.290
like it's the hot take that basically travels

955
00:39:11.290 --> 00:39:12.710
and that's what we're trafficking in.

956
00:39:12.710 --> 00:39:15.070
But I think it is important to point out,

957
00:39:15.070 --> 00:39:17.350
as you astutely noted a moment ago,

958
00:39:17.350 --> 00:39:20.230
that most people are not in this space.

959
00:39:20.230 --> 00:39:22.090
Like, we're kind of in the middle,

960
00:39:22.090 --> 00:39:24.800
we're trying to figure out what's true and what's not.

961
00:39:24.800 --> 00:39:27.950
And give us a little bit credit

962
00:39:27.950 --> 00:39:30.053
when it comes to discernment, right?

963
00:39:32.980 --> 00:39:35.633
Over the course of my sabbatical,

964
00:39:36.590 --> 00:39:39.890
I did spend a fair amount of time

965
00:39:39.890 --> 00:39:44.690
trying to make sense for myself of this world

966
00:39:44.690 --> 00:39:49.690
that feels at times like it's losing its grip on reality,

967
00:39:50.410 --> 00:39:53.423
depending upon what your information bubble looks like.

968
00:39:55.020 --> 00:40:00.020
So on the subject of the sort of polar extremes

969
00:40:01.460 --> 00:40:06.380
on the one hand, are, we could hold the perspective,

970
00:40:06.380 --> 00:40:10.440
are people and institutions flawed and sometimes mistaken?

971
00:40:10.440 --> 00:40:12.300
Does science make mistakes

972
00:40:12.300 --> 00:40:14.450
or does science, from time to time,

973
00:40:14.450 --> 00:40:16.960
change their mind when new information comes in?

974
00:40:16.960 --> 00:40:18.610
Does the scientific,

975
00:40:18.610 --> 00:40:21.850
does the consensus scientific community screw up

976
00:40:21.850 --> 00:40:23.700
and at times air egregiously

977
00:40:23.700 --> 00:40:27.280
when it comes to messaging the populous?

978
00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:29.610
Are the incentives of the media misaligned?

979
00:40:29.610 --> 00:40:32.240
Do we have serious problems in government, tech, media,

980
00:40:32.240 --> 00:40:34.950
and at times science?

981
00:40:34.950 --> 00:40:38.280
Like, I would agree that all of those things are true.

982
00:40:38.280 --> 00:40:43.020
Or is there a secret psyops event

983
00:40:43.020 --> 00:40:45.330
of untold proportions afoot

984
00:40:45.330 --> 00:40:49.520
where this cabal of organized evil is organizing

985
00:40:49.520 --> 00:40:53.700
to control our minds and our bodies?

986
00:40:53.700 --> 00:40:54.533
Yes.

987
00:40:54.533 --> 00:40:55.891
Is that true also?

988
00:40:55.891 --> 00:40:57.450
I mean, no way, that's not true.

989
00:40:57.450 --> 00:40:59.790
Maybe part of that is true, I don't know.

990
00:40:59.790 --> 00:41:00.890
Probably not.

991
00:41:01.750 --> 00:41:05.650
But this idea that either, like, we should just

992
00:41:09.310 --> 00:41:13.550
give Anthony Fauci a crown and name all our pets Fauci

993
00:41:13.550 --> 00:41:18.460
and just put him on our t-shirts and lay down at his feet,

994
00:41:18.460 --> 00:41:22.853
or there's a crazy conspiracy afoot of mind control.

995
00:41:24.460 --> 00:41:25.293
Right.

996
00:41:25.293 --> 00:41:26.360
Are people naming their dogs Fauci,

997
00:41:26.360 --> 00:41:27.610
'cause that is a dog name.

998
00:41:27.610 --> 00:41:29.146
Yeah, that's a thing.

999
00:41:29.146 --> 00:41:29.979
That's a thing?
For sure.

1000
00:41:29.979 --> 00:41:30.812
A lot of people are doing that.

1001
00:41:30.812 --> 00:41:31.645
Okay.

1002
00:41:31.645 --> 00:41:32.478
I didn't realize he was worth it.

1003
00:41:32.478 --> 00:41:35.380
So listen, live in the gray

1004
00:41:35.380 --> 00:41:39.460
and I live in the nuance and I defer to that former idea,

1005
00:41:39.460 --> 00:41:44.460
which is that there are scientists who are working hard

1006
00:41:45.110 --> 00:41:47.230
to solve a very difficult problem,

1007
00:41:47.230 --> 00:41:51.490
and they're doing it anonymously and imperfectly,

1008
00:41:51.490 --> 00:41:53.270
and the messaging isn't always great,

1009
00:41:53.270 --> 00:41:54.810
and there's been lots of flubs,

1010
00:41:54.810 --> 00:41:57.530
and there's reason to distrust the media.

1011
00:41:57.530 --> 00:41:59.190
And I don't wanna spend a lot of time on this.

1012
00:41:59.190 --> 00:42:02.070
I don't wanna go down some crazy vaccine rabbit hole.

1013
00:42:02.070 --> 00:42:04.320
I really don't wanna dwell on this very long.

1014
00:42:04.320 --> 00:42:05.900
I am, like I said at the outset,

1015
00:42:05.900 --> 00:42:07.700
reluctant to even bring it up

1016
00:42:07.700 --> 00:42:10.060
because it is so unbelievably divisive

1017
00:42:10.060 --> 00:42:11.800
and because whatever I say

1018
00:42:11.800 --> 00:42:13.750
is unlikely to change anyone's mind.

1019
00:42:13.750 --> 00:42:16.520
But I do feel that it is important to say

1020
00:42:16.520 --> 00:42:18.507
that although there have been mistakes

1021
00:42:18.507 --> 00:42:23.507
and there's been overreach, I'm not in favor of mandates

1022
00:42:25.076 --> 00:42:27.180
and I think that there's been a lot of errors made

1023
00:42:27.180 --> 00:42:31.240
in terms of kids in schools and what's going on there,

1024
00:42:31.240 --> 00:42:34.330
and I understand the problems of Big Pharma

1025
00:42:34.330 --> 00:42:35.820
and the misaligned incentives there,

1026
00:42:35.820 --> 00:42:38.250
but I do, like I said, believe that there are good people,

1027
00:42:38.250 --> 00:42:40.630
good scientists who are trying to solve

1028
00:42:40.630 --> 00:42:42.660
difficult problems imperfectly.

1029
00:42:42.660 --> 00:42:46.163
And as for the Rogan kind of Spotify situation specifically,

1030
00:42:47.320 --> 00:42:48.820
I'm not into deep platforming,

1031
00:42:48.820 --> 00:42:50.120
I don't think that's a solution.

1032
00:42:50.120 --> 00:42:52.780
I don't think that he should be punted off Spotify.

1033
00:42:52.780 --> 00:42:56.710
And I think this goes back to this issue of incentives.

1034
00:42:56.710 --> 00:43:01.710
There are incentives to host heterodox thinkers

1035
00:43:02.580 --> 00:43:06.310
and there are incentives to be heterodox in your thinking.

1036
00:43:06.310 --> 00:43:10.450
And I think heterodoxy is very appealing to many right now,

1037
00:43:10.450 --> 00:43:12.460
especially with this degraded trust

1038
00:43:12.460 --> 00:43:14.650
in media and institutions

1039
00:43:14.650 --> 00:43:18.230
and even more so when that heterodox thinking

1040
00:43:18.230 --> 00:43:19.840
entails a conspiracy.

1041
00:43:19.840 --> 00:43:23.350
There's something about our neurochemistry that lights up,

1042
00:43:23.350 --> 00:43:25.290
suddenly the world makes sense.

1043
00:43:25.290 --> 00:43:27.930
And when you combine that with this media distrust,

1044
00:43:27.930 --> 00:43:29.740
it creates an interesting

1045
00:43:29.740 --> 00:43:32.620
and, at times, problematic scenario.

1046
00:43:32.620 --> 00:43:36.830
But the truth is just because you are heterodox

1047
00:43:36.830 --> 00:43:39.180
does not mean that you are correct.

1048
