but more like who are the people that are accessible to me

2570
01:48:32.130 --> 01:48:36.900
who can provide me guidance, wisdom, goalpost

2571
01:48:36.900 --> 01:48:38.640
on things that I'm struggling with?

2572
01:48:38.640 --> 01:48:42.260
And those are just regular people that are in my life.

2573
01:48:42.260 --> 01:48:45.220
I would add to that guests that I've had on the podcast,

2574
01:48:45.220 --> 01:48:46.940
like I'll reflect back on a conversation

2575
01:48:46.940 --> 01:48:48.080
that I've had with somebody.

2576
01:48:48.080 --> 01:48:49.930
'Cause the people that come on the show

2577
01:48:49.930 --> 01:48:51.530
are people that I wanna learn from,

2578
01:48:51.530 --> 01:48:53.130
perhaps I'm going through something

2579
01:48:53.130 --> 01:48:56.440
and I bring on this expert and they help me

2580
01:48:56.440 --> 01:48:59.840
kind of process in real time how to solve a certain problem

2581
01:48:59.840 --> 01:49:02.610
or think about a certain situation.

2582
01:49:02.610 --> 01:49:05.390
And some of those people had become friends,

2583
01:49:05.390 --> 01:49:08.330
so I can call upon them when I'm in need.

2584
01:49:08.330 --> 01:49:09.830
But I would say, more often than not,

2585
01:49:09.830 --> 01:49:11.507
like the people that inspire me

2586
01:49:11.507 --> 01:49:13.650
are like regular people that I have in my life,

2587
01:49:13.650 --> 01:49:14.640
like anonymous people.

2588
01:49:14.640 --> 01:49:16.360
Like, I'm going through a particular,

2589
01:49:16.360 --> 01:49:18.330
I'm trying to make a decision about a certain thing.

2590
01:49:18.330 --> 01:49:20.990
So I have a friend who's really good

2591
01:49:20.990 --> 01:49:22.450
at that kind of decision-making

2592
01:49:22.450 --> 01:49:24.220
and that's the person that I call.

2593
01:49:24.220 --> 01:49:26.380
Or I'm having a relationship thing,

2594
01:49:26.380 --> 01:49:27.960
or I'm having a professional thing,

2595
01:49:27.960 --> 01:49:29.660
or I'm having a sobriety thing.

2596
01:49:29.660 --> 01:49:33.730
Like, I have buckets with different people

2597
01:49:33.730 --> 01:49:37.220
for all of those different kind of aspects of life

2598
01:49:37.220 --> 01:49:39.081
that we all come across.

2599
01:49:39.081 --> 01:49:40.347
So I don't think, I'm like,

2600
01:49:40.347 --> 01:49:43.300
"Oh, that person that I put up on a pedestal."

2601
01:49:43.300 --> 01:49:44.970
I mean, one thing I've learned

2602
01:49:44.970 --> 01:49:49.970
in doing this for so many years is people are people, man.

2603
01:49:50.190 --> 01:49:55.190
Like, I've had some pretty fancy people come

2604
01:49:55.330 --> 01:49:57.010
and sit across from me on this podcast,

2605
01:49:57.010 --> 01:49:58.986
and that's always exciting--
Thank you.

2606
01:49:58.986 --> 01:49:59.819
And I get nervous.

2607
01:49:59.819 --> 01:50:00.652
Oh, thank you, thank you.

2608
01:50:00.652 --> 01:50:02.840
You're not one of those people.

2609
01:50:02.840 --> 01:50:04.093
Of course you are.

2610
01:50:04.093 --> 01:50:04.926
You don't have to say that.

2611
01:50:04.926 --> 01:50:06.660
And then you spend a couple of hours with them

2612
01:50:06.660 --> 01:50:08.190
and you're like, "Oh, it's just a guy.

2613
01:50:08.190 --> 01:50:09.137
Oh, just a," whatever.

2614
01:50:09.137 --> 01:50:11.330
And then you're like, "Well, if that's just a guy,

2615
01:50:11.330 --> 01:50:13.640
then that other person that I'm thinking about

2616
01:50:13.640 --> 01:50:15.290
in this really spectacular way,

2617
01:50:15.290 --> 01:50:18.410
well, they're just a human being too," right?

2618
01:50:18.410 --> 01:50:22.230
It really helps round you in that realization.

2619
01:50:22.230 --> 01:50:26.920
So that sort of cured me of a lot of hero worship.

2620
01:50:26.920 --> 01:50:31.920
So I draw my inspiration from all places.

2621
01:50:31.980 --> 01:50:35.620
And I think, for me, the most inspiring people

2622
01:50:35.620 --> 01:50:38.320
are kind of the anonymous heroes

2623
01:50:38.320 --> 01:50:39.990
who are doing amazing things

2624
01:50:39.990 --> 01:50:42.924
and not seeking attention for it.

2625
01:50:42.924 --> 01:50:44.600
Thank you.
There you are again.

2626
01:50:44.600 --> 01:50:45.972
You keep cropping up.

2627
01:50:45.972 --> 01:50:47.110
(Adam laughs)

2628
01:50:47.110 --> 01:50:49.197
You're everywhere.
I know.

2629
01:50:49.197 --> 01:50:52.318
You're like termites, crawling out of the wood.

2630
01:50:52.318 --> 01:50:53.970
I'm not asking for this adulation.

2631
01:50:53.970 --> 01:50:55.340
How badly do you want it, Adam?

2632
01:50:55.340 --> 01:50:57.590
