01:54:52.723 --> 01:54:54.365
This is your wife calling you.

2714
01:54:54.365 --> 01:54:55.467
(Adam laughs)

2715
01:54:55.467 --> 01:54:58.670
Were there no other voicemails on the service?

2716
01:54:58.670 --> 01:55:00.040
You're like--

2717
01:55:00.040 --> 01:55:01.470
There were.

2718
01:55:01.470 --> 01:55:04.270
She wanted in, so I gave him, come on, guys.

2719
01:55:04.270 --> 01:55:07.257
Come on, listeners, you got to indulge me on this one.

2720
01:55:07.257 --> 01:55:09.150
Let me make this easy for April.

2721
01:55:09.150 --> 01:55:12.580
April, you're feeling like you're in a bit of a slump?

2722
01:55:12.580 --> 01:55:15.670
That has to be because of Adam.

2723
01:55:15.670 --> 01:55:16.530
This is your fault.

2724
01:55:16.530 --> 01:55:18.048
It's clearly, clearly.

2725
01:55:18.048 --> 01:55:20.250
What are you doing to contribute to April's slump?

2726
01:55:20.250 --> 01:55:22.160
It's what I'm not doing, Rich.

2727
01:55:22.160 --> 01:55:23.590
Clearly.

2728
01:55:23.590 --> 01:55:24.910
You're the issue here.

2729
01:55:24.910 --> 01:55:27.130
It has nothing to do with running.

2730
01:55:27.130 --> 01:55:28.980
Are you showing up as a husband?

2731
01:55:28.980 --> 01:55:30.690
Let's make this about you.

2732
01:55:30.690 --> 01:55:32.021
Wait, wait, what?

2733
01:55:32.021 --> 01:55:34.438
(both laugh)

2734
01:55:36.090 --> 01:55:39.223
Listen, April, thank you for your question.

2735
01:55:40.190 --> 01:55:43.570
You've been running for six months, five days a week,

2736
01:55:43.570 --> 01:55:45.760
of course you're feeling like maybe

2737
01:55:45.760 --> 01:55:47.350
less than enthusiastic about it.

2738
01:55:47.350 --> 01:55:48.810
These things have to have a season.

2739
01:55:48.810 --> 01:55:50.350
Take a break, first of all,

2740
01:55:50.350 --> 01:55:52.790
before you make any drastic decisions

2741
01:55:52.790 --> 01:55:54.923
about your future as a runner.

2742
01:55:56.260 --> 01:55:59.283
Every athlete needs breaks.

2743
01:56:00.350 --> 01:56:02.760
So if you're worried about losing

2744
01:56:02.760 --> 01:56:03.720
the fitness that you gained,

2745
01:56:03.720 --> 01:56:05.100
let's try to do something else,

2746
01:56:05.100 --> 01:56:07.300
movement-oriented for a couple of weeks

2747
01:56:07.300 --> 01:56:09.810
and allow your body to kind of reset.

2748
01:56:09.810 --> 01:56:13.950
I mean, going six months, five days a week of running,

2749
01:56:13.950 --> 01:56:18.950
that's gonna give any runner a sort of malaise over it.

2750
01:56:19.860 --> 01:56:22.380
So I think that's number one.

2751
01:56:23.590 --> 01:56:27.020
The second thing is you don't have to be a runner.

2752
01:56:27.020 --> 01:56:29.050
Like, you're not a professional runner.

2753
01:56:29.050 --> 01:56:31.610
So if it's not doing it for you anymore,

2754
01:56:31.610 --> 01:56:35.530
you can feel free to switch it up

2755
01:56:35.530 --> 01:56:38.750
and find something else that you enjoy doing.

2756
01:56:38.750 --> 01:56:41.300
But before you do that, take that break

2757
01:56:41.300 --> 01:56:43.200
and then return to running

2758
01:56:43.200 --> 01:56:45.700
and maybe put something on the calendar,

2759
01:56:45.700 --> 01:56:49.950
find something within running that scares you or excites you

2760
01:56:49.950 --> 01:56:53.130
and set yourself up for a bit of an adventure

2761
01:56:53.130 --> 01:56:56.070
and that might inject your running experience

2762
01:56:56.070 --> 01:56:59.310
with a little bit more excitement and enthusiasm.

2763
01:56:59.310 --> 01:57:00.920
'Cause it sounds like you're just kinda doing it

2764
01:57:00.920 --> 01:57:02.100
to do it now.

2765
01:57:02.100 --> 01:57:04.790
You achieve these goals of running two half marathons,

2766
01:57:04.790 --> 01:57:06.290
congratulations, by the way.

2767
01:57:06.290 --> 01:57:07.523
Very quickly, too.

2768
01:57:07.523 --> 01:57:09.410
So is there another race,

2769
01:57:09.410 --> 01:57:11.210
like what's the backstory here, Adam?

2770
01:57:11.210 --> 01:57:12.730
Like, is there another race on the calendar?

2771
01:57:12.730 --> 01:57:16.090
What else is, first of all, you have a baby too.

2772
01:57:16.090 --> 01:57:17.770
So there's a lot going on.

2773
01:57:17.770 --> 01:57:19.512
Yeah, he's a toddler now.

2774
01:57:19.512 --> 01:57:20.850
She's done amazing.

2775
01:57:20.850 --> 01:57:23.453
She's like in incredible shape.

2776
01:57:24.350 --> 01:57:26.950
She ran the Malibu half in under 1:50.

2777
01:57:26.950 --> 01:57:29.730
She just ran another sub-two hour.

2778
01:57:29.730 --> 01:57:32.250
We had the Pasadena marathon, half marathon

2779
01:57:32.250 --> 01:57:34.720
and then the Ventura half marathon on the calendar,

2780
01:57:34.720 --> 01:57:38.170
but with omicron and just being with a toddler at home,

2781
01:57:38.170 --> 01:57:40.920
we are just not equipped to like going into the public

2782
01:57:40.920 --> 01:57:43.480
and breathing on each other quite yet.

2783
01:57:43.480 --> 01:57:45.007
So we didn't do Pasedena,

2784
01:57:45.007 --> 01:57:46.840
and she's not sure she's gonna do Ventura.

2785
01:57:46.840 --> 01:57:48.100
But she did it the same day.

2786
01:57:48.100 --> 01:57:49.540
She did her own course.

2787
01:57:49.540 --> 01:57:54.470
I had, like you, had a back injury, so I had to back out.

2788
01:57:54.470 --> 01:57:57.450
But we were gonna do, she was gonna be my partner

2789
01:57:57.450 --> 01:58:01.070
in the Otillo Catalina race, but that just got postponed.

2790
01:58:01.070 --> 01:58:03.440
So that was the plan, is do this half marathon

2791
01:58:03.440 --> 01:58:05.230
and then start getting in the water with me

2792
01:58:05.230 --> 01:58:08.550
and doing trails with me and doing Otilla,

2793
01:58:08.550 --> 01:58:09.830
but that just got postponed again.

2794
01:58:09.830 --> 01:58:12.430
So that's the backstory.

2795
01:58:12.430 --> 01:58:13.630
Yeah, okay.

2796
01:58:13.630 --> 01:58:18.630
So yeah, find something, take a break,

2797
01:58:19.610 --> 01:58:23.460
let yourself breathe, maintain your fitness in another way,

2798
01:58:23.460 --> 01:58:26.870
come back to it with something to put on the calendar

2799
01:58:26.870 --> 01:58:29.100
that would get you excited, that would be fun.

2800
01:58:29.100 --> 01:58:30.770
It doesn't have to be, even a race,

2801
01:58:30.770 --> 01:58:32.790
it could just be some kind of adventure

2802
01:58:32.790 --> 01:58:34.240
that you create for yourself.

2803
01:58:35.280 --> 01:58:38.190
And also, maybe try to make it communal,

2804
01:58:38.190 --> 01:58:41.540
like join a run club or meet some new people

2805
01:58:41.540 --> 01:58:44.736
to go running with or mix it up.

2806
01:58:44.736 --> 01:58:48.370
Go run someplace that you haven't run before,

2807
01:58:48.370 --> 01:58:51.570
like, I would make that suggestion

2808
01:58:51.570 --> 01:58:52.620
'cause you want it to be fun.

2809
01:58:52.620 --> 01:58:55.530
But the flip side of that is, like, you were,

2810
01:58:55.530 --> 01:58:56.770
we were talking about this earlier,

2811
01:58:56.770 --> 01:58:58.490
you're like, "I don't run 'cause it's fun.

2812
01:58:58.490 --> 01:58:59.730
Like, I run 'cause it's hard

2813
01:58:59.730 --> 01:59:01.730
and, like, I just do this thing," right?

2814
01:59:02.711 --> 01:59:03.560
It doesn't have to be fun.

2815
01:59:03.560 --> 01:59:06.780
You just do it and you push through these temporary phases

2816
01:59:06.780 --> 01:59:08.990
and these phases shift and change.

2817
01:59:08.990 --> 01:59:10.280
But I think the fact that,

2818
01:59:10.280 --> 01:59:12.750
April, you've been doing it for six months without a break,

2819
01:59:12.750 --> 01:59:14.100
like you're due for a break,

2820
01:59:14.100 --> 01:59:16.710
take that break and do it guilt-free.

2821
01:59:16.710 --> 01:59:18.470
Beautiful, I love it.

2822
01:59:18.470 --> 01:59:20.750
But April is a person who's like the type

2823
01:59:20.750 --> 01:59:22.500
that has like a favorite thing

2824
01:59:22.500 --> 01:59:24.300
and then she could just go off it, like,

2825
01:59:24.300 --> 01:59:25.940
which is amazing that I've stuck around,

2826
01:59:25.940 --> 01:59:28.141
that she's allowed me to stay.

2827
01:59:28.141 --> 01:59:29.510
Like, I hope that--

2828
01:59:29.510 --> 01:59:33.785
Like, she's a test case in David Epstein's book range,

2829
01:59:33.785 --> 01:59:36.660
just like, "I'm trying new things," good.

2830
01:59:36.660 --> 01:59:37.493
But also because she's--

2831
01:59:37.493 --> 01:59:38.880
You don't have to be a lifelong runner.

2832
01:59:38.880 --> 01:59:41.780
Like she's so good at like almost everything she picks up.

2833
01:59:41.780 --> 01:59:43.010
So that's also the other thing.

2834
01:59:43.010 --> 01:59:44.270
Yeah, I think when people are that,

2835
01:59:44.270 --> 01:59:46.850
have that kind of aptitude for almost anything,

2836
01:59:46.850 --> 01:59:48.350
that probably happens, I would say.

2837
01:59:48.350 --> 01:59:49.183
Must be nice.

2838
01:59:49.183 --> 01:59:50.487
Yeah, must be nice.

2839
01:59:50.487 --> 01:59:53.490
(both laugh)

2840
01:59:53.490 --> 01:59:55.700
All right, I think we did it.

2841
01:59:55.700 --> 01:59:56.533
We did it, man.

2842
01:59:56.533 --> 01:59:57.390
How do you feel?

2843
01:59:58.380 --> 01:59:59.213
I feel good.

2844
01:59:59.213 --> 02:00:02.570
